362910786644e-05],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,2403,315,279,42446,304,279,7071,323,279,8622,12371,6113,525,3232,42939,13,16246,429,57960,1975,1056,90,1706,31716,374,220,18,8153,1293,11,1246,1657,9334,8153,11,13302,304,44548,17855,1352,11,525,304,279,3082,315,279,4453,6774,30,508,6405,921,474,297,13842,62944,26,1159,17047,26,1159,4771,26,1379,7,16,20,15,1215,1638,2752,2333,258,28357,7,15,13,23,1106,12670,1294,17228,280,1958,1548,600,284,220,15,26,600,366,220,21,26,3443,72,12798,13030,989,60,284,5419,7,18,15,488,220,21,15,23019,317,532,7633,65792,58,15,60,313,13030,58,17,60,313,13030,58,19,60,313,21621,317,7633,65792,58,16,60,313,13030,58,18,60,313,13030,58,20,60,313,21621,317,1502,20912,35,73315,13030,58,15,1125,3944,1215,2383,20912,34,73315,13030,58,16,1125,45,1215,2383,20912,33,73315,13030,58,17,1125,69214,1215,2383,20912,32,73315,13030,58,18,1125,16844,317,1502,20912,37,73315,13030,58,19,1125,50,1215,2383,20912,36,73315,13030,58,20,1125,925,317,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nAll of the triangles in the figure and the central hexagon are equilateral. Given that $\\overline{AC}$ is 3 units long, how many square units, expressed in simplest radical form, are in the area of the entire star? [asy]\nimport olympiad; import geometry; import graph; size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));\npair[] vertices;\nfor(int i = 0; i < 6; ++i){\n\nvertices[i] = dir(30 + 60*i);\n}\ndraw(vertices[0]--vertices[2]--vertices[4]--cycle);\ndraw(vertices[1]--vertices[3]--vertices[5]--cycle);\nlabel(\"$D$\",vertices[0],NE); label(\"$C$\",vertices[1],N); label(\"$B$\",vertices[2],NW); label(\"$A$\",vertices[3],SW);\nlabel(\"$F$\",vertices[4],S); label(\"$E$\",vertices[5],SE);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"fb98ec97ffbc1747ab50d81f4454b2a4067298d8aa503ecf44a5971975db53f0"},"seconds":38.05045795440674,"seed":825061309745592218,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we will first find the area of the central hexagon and the area of the six equilateral triangles that form the points of the star. Then, we will sum these areas to get the total area of the star.\n\n1. **Calculate the side length of the central hexagon:**\n\n   Since $\\overline{AC}$ is given as 3 units and the central hexagon is equilateral, we recognize that $\\overline{AC}$ spans two side lengths of the hexagon. Therefore, each side of the hexagon is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{3}{2} = 1.5 \\text{ units}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Area of the central hexagon:**\n\n   The area of an equilateral triangle with side length \\( s \\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} s^2\n   \\]\n   The hexagon can be divided into 6 such triangles, so the area of the hexagon is:\n   \\[\n   6 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\left(1.5\\right)^2 = 6 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 2.25 = 6 \\times \\frac{2.25\\sqrt{3}}{4} = 6 \\times 0.5625\\sqrt{3} = 3.375\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Area of one of the six equilateral triangles forming the star:**\n\n   Each of these triangles has a side length equal to the side length of the hexagon, which is 1.5 units. Thus, the area of one such triangle is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\left(1.5\\right)^2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 2.25 = \\frac{2.25\\sqrt{3}}{4} = 0.5625\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total area of the six outer triangles:**\n\n   There are six such triangles, so their total area is:\n   \\[\n   6 \\times 0.5625\\sqrt{3} = 3.375\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Total area of the star:**\n\n   The total area of the star is the sum of the area of the central hexagon and the area of the six outer triangles:\n   \\[\n   3.375\\sqrt{3} + 3.375\\sqrt{3} = 6.75\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total area of the star is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6.75\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6.75\\sqrt{3}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
